# Corpus Studio — local development credentials.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored and stays on your machine;
# API_KEYS is a REAL credential, so never commit it or paste it into an issue.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The app normally reads `gateway.env` from userData, and
# that file is fragile in a way a checkout is not: `e2e/settings.spec.ts`
# isolates the DB path but NOT userData, so running the suite overwrites it with
# test literals — after which every analysis returns 403 and each paper reports
# "carries nothing", which reads as a model problem rather than a wiped key.
# This copy survives that, and survives wiping userData to test first-run.
#
# PRECEDENCE, lowest last:
#   1. CORPUS_LLM_URL / CORPUS_LLM_KEY   (env vars — a launch script or a test)
#   2. userData/gateway.env              (what Settings writes)
#   3. this file
# So anything typed in Settings still wins; this only answers when nothing else
# does. A packaged build never reads it — there is no repo root to find.

# The llm-communicator gateway. Loopback: the container publishes on the host,
# and the endpoint the app appends to is `/api/chat/completions`.
BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080

# The gateway's own API key, from its container config.
API_KEYS=replace-me
